        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Darleen Carr, Charmian Carr, Charles Napier\n- Roles: Margaret Devlin, Luther Sprague, Liesl\n- Works: The Oregon Trail, The Sound of Music\n\nFacts:\n- Charmian Carr was born as Charmian Anne Farnon on December 27, 1942.\n- Darleen Carr was born as Darlene Farnon on December 12, 1950.\n- Charmian Carr was an American actress and singer.\n- In the 1965 film version of The Sound of Music, Charmian Carr was best known for playing Liesl, the eldest Von Trapp daughter.\n- Darleen Carr is an American actress, singer, and voice-over artist.\n- In the TV series The Oregon Trail, Darleen Carr stars as Margaret Devlin, a passenger on the wagon train.\n- In the TV series The Oregon Trail, Charles Napier portrays Luther Sprague, a frontier scout recruited by Thorpe.\n- Charmian Carr died on September 17, 2016.",
